-- title:
--   Place realising a height-one prime at a supersingular node
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, an integer $N \ge 1$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$; fix modular polynomial data `data` of level $q$ (a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ vanishing on the pair $(j, j_q)$) satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (Y^q - X)(Y - X^q)$ modulo $q$, and proofs $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ that the Hecke maps $\overline{\alpha}$, $\overline{\beta}$ of level $N$ and index $q$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ are integral ring homomorphisms. Given a place specialisation $P$ for these data and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$ (in particular a regular prolongation $R.R_1$ of $A$ to the level-$Nq$ function field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-field `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)`, with residue map `R.residue₁` into the level-$N$ function field `modularFunctionFieldC k N` over $k$), assume $q \nmid N$ and $\mathrm{red}$ surjective. Let $K/\mathbb{Q}$ be a finite subextension of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $w$ be a place of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` lying in `ssPlaces q N k`, i.e. satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace q N k w`, and let $C =$ `jIntegralClosure (N * q) A K`, the ring of elements of the subfield `fieldOver (N * q) K` of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((X))$ generated by the constants of $K$ together with $j$ and $j_{Nq}$ that are integral over `jRing A K`. Let $\mathfrak{p} \subset C$ be a prime ideal of height $1$ with the image of $q$ not in $\mathfrak{p}$, and assume that for every $t$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` whose Laurent series lies in $C$ and represents an element of $\mathfrak{p}$, the element $t$ lies in the valuation subring $R.R_1.\mathrm{integers}$ and `R.residue₁` of $t$ has value $0$ at $w$ (it lies in the valuation subring of $w$ and its residue is $0$). The conclusion is that there is a place $W$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — a proper valuation subring containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose underlying ring is a principal ideal ring — such that: (i) for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` whose Laurent series lies in `fieldOver (N * q) K`, one has $g \in \mathcal{O}_W$ if and only if $g s = r$ for some $r, s \in C$ with $s \notin \mathfrak{p}$; and (ii) for every $t$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` whose Laurent series lies in $C$ there is $a \in A$ with $W$ taking the value $a$ at $t$, and such that $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ precisely when $t \in R.R_1.\mathrm{integers}$ and `R.residue₁` of $t$ has value $0$ at $w$.
--
--   This is the level-$Nq$ statement that a horizontal height-one prime of the normalisation $C$ of `jRing A K` in the level-$Nq$ function field over $K$, lying over the supersingular place $w$ of the level-$N$ fibre, is cut out by a place $W$ of the function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose centre reduces into $A$; clause (i) identifies $\mathcal{O}_W \cap$ `fieldOver (N * q) K` with the localisation $C_{\mathfrak{p}}$, and clause (ii) matches vanishing at the node with the maximal ideal of $A$. It is used in the study of the local rings `nodeIntegersOver` at the nodes of the reduction of $X_0(Nq)$ at $q$ — their Noetherianity, locality, and the description of elements of those rings by multiplicative relations in $C$.
